        "names_and_negations": true,
        "lexical_fidelity": true,
        "uncertainties_disclosed": false
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "τὴν κραυγὴν αὐτῶν τὴν ἐρχομένην πρὸς μὲ",
          "english_quote": "the outcry from them that comes to me",
          "issue": "“From them” selects a source or subjective interpretation of αὐτῶν. An outcry concerning or against them is also a material contextual interpretation, especially in the discussion of Sodom's destruction. The existing note discusses the completion verb but does not disclose this genitive ambiguity. The selected main rendering is defensible; the problem is incomplete disclosure, not an unsupported main claim.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a source-quoted note explaining the choice of “from them” and preserving “the outcry concerning/against them that comes to me” as an alternative. Alternatively, consider the more source-transparent “their outcry that comes to me,” still documenting the potentially different relationships expressed by the genitive.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "συντελοῦνται",
          "english_quote": "they are carrying things through",
          "issue": "The main text adopts an action-oriented understanding of the middle/passive form. The note acknowledges completion and unexpressed conduct, but does not distinguish that understanding from an intransitive or passive completion reading, such as their reaching an end or being brought to an end. Those readings change the subject's role and are therefore material alternatives. The printed form itself is not evidence of an OCR defect.",
          "suggested_revision": "Expand the note to identify the middle/passive form, explain the contextual basis for the action-oriented rendering, and preserve the viable completion/end reading as an alternative. Do not substitute an active Greek form or import a different edition's quotation.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "3.40",
      "verdict": "accept",
      "checks": {
