      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": true,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "lexical_fidelity": true,
        "uncertainties_disclosed": false
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "πρότερον διαλεχθῆναί με αὐτοῖς, εἶθ’ οὕτως κἀκεῖνον ἐπισκέψασθαι δύνασθαι αὐτόν.",
          "english_quote": "that I speak with them first; afterward I could visit him too.",
          "issue": "The first infinitival clause explicitly uses με, whereas the final construction contains the third-person accusative αὐτόν alongside κἀκεῖνον. Continuing with “I” is contextually defensible as a reported reference to the narrator, but the draft silently normalizes the change of person and gives no account of the final pronoun's attachment or referent. The uncertainty concerns the printed construction, not unverified ink.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a source-quoted note explaining that the main text understands the final αὐτόν as a reported reference to the narrator, with ἐκεῖνον referring to Apion, because the surrounding request concerns the narrator's speaking and proposed visit. Disclose that αὐτόν is formally third person and that alternative subject/object attachments leave the visitor's identity less secure. Preserve the supplied αὐτόν rather than silently correcting it to με. Also retain the sequencing force of οὕτως, for example with “after doing that, I could visit him too.”",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
